Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"9cea1130-c48a-5546-a13c-956b38e5b4a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"926f417d-c104-164a-8a03-0171227bd6eb"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"4d262d9a-9c98-3148-a9d7-bd2b3b75b176"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"6a197df3-73b4-244d-8757-98659003f356"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"452c0a71-9f4b-3047-a9e7-49fce0bfb206"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"28503bcd-1fd0-6745-afaf-465bad9c3aff"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ca53b0a2-1f39-ca48-b705-b7df3d53e3b7"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"87079b82-417b-554a-badd-c14bade942ad"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"573e644c-79a0-494b-9c38-5d331b192f56"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"87efd9b7-e626-f242-a896-ee219f2a8961"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"60c06e93-430e-4340-82ef-3a9efcbf8093"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"afd2cbf5-2dcf-2745-9bfd-b062b5dd9eb5"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"eeeba95d-a927-274e-bbd3-112843310368"],

